{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal property unit conversion thermal property unit conversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","fileName":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Temperature Readings versus Intervals","Compound Rate Unit Conversion","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal property unit conversion thermal property unit conversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","fileName":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion","heading":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Thermal-property units combine energy or power with area, length, mass, and temperature intervals in different positions. The book writes thermal conductivity in W/(m·K), heat-transfer coefficient in W/(m²·K), heat capacity in kJ/K, and specific heat capacity in kJ/(kg·K). These are not one interchangeable heat unit: the extra length, area, or mass changes the dimension. In compound conversions, Fahrenheit-to-kelvin interval ratios are multiplicative; the absolute-temperature offset is not inserted into a denominator. See [[Temperature Readings versus Intervals]] and [[Compound Rate Unit Conversion]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Temperature Readings versus Intervals","Compound Rate Unit Conversion","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal property unit conversion thermal property unit conversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","fileName":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Property Unit Conversion","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Temperature Readings versus Intervals","Compound Rate Unit Conversion","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}